Subject: [PATCH] WebRTC: treat maxFramerate as an upper bound

A 15 fps camera must remain usable when the application requests a maximum
of 20 fps. A fixed framerate forces drop-only videorate to increase the rate
and causes not-negotiated when replacing the placeholder with the camera.

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerVideoRTPPacketizer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerVideoRTPPacketizer.cpp
@@ -203,7 +203,8 @@
             int numerator, denominator;
             gst_util_double_to_fraction(static_cast<double>(maxFrameRate), &numerator, &denominator);

-            auto caps = adoptGRef(gst_caps_new_simple("video/x-raw", "framerate", GST_TYPE_FRACTION, numerator, denominator, nullptr));
+            // maxFramerate is a ceiling; drop-only videorate cannot increase a slower capture rate.
+            auto caps = adoptGRef(gst_caps_new_simple("video/x-raw", "framerate", GST_TYPE_FRACTION_RANGE, 0, 1, numerator, denominator, nullptr));
             g_object_set(m_frameRateCapsFilter.get(), "caps", caps.get(), nullptr);
         }
     }
